<title>USA: Value City Q2 shr $0.40 vs $0.51.</title>
<headline>Value City Q2 shr $0.40 vs $0.51.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in millions except per share data)</p>
<p>			    Second Quarter Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>		     2/01/97	2/03/96    2/01/97	2/03/96</p>
<p>			 13 wks	14 wks     26 wks	 27 wks</p>
<p> NET SALES (a)     $323.0	$296.4     $589.1	 $514.2</p>
<p> NET INCOME	    12.9	  16.2	 18.6	   18.7</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER</p>
<p>   SHARE		 0.40	  0.51	 0.58	   0.59</p>
<p>AVERAGE SHARES</p>
<p>   OUTSTANDING (b)   31.7	  31.7	 31.7	   31.8</p>
<p>SHARES USED FOR</p>
<p>FULLY DILUTED</p>
<p>   EPS (b)	     32.3	  31.7	 32.3	   31.8</p>
<p>(a)  In the prior year, the Company changed its fiscal year end to the Saturday closest to July 31 to conform to the National Retail Federation's suggested retail calendar.  This change added one week to the three and six month periods ended February 3, 1996. (b)  Excludes 368,600 Treasury Shares at February 1, 1997 and February 3, 1996.</p>
<p>FULL CO NAME: Value City Department Stores Inc.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
